+
+## Recovery
+
+Protect the Harnie store before risky operations. Use `harnie backup <path>`
+to write a consistent SQLite snapshot of the live store. The output file is
+created owner-read/write (`0600`).
+
+```sh
+harnie backup "$HARNIE_HOME/harnie.db.bak"
+```
+
+Use `harnie restore <path> --force` to return to a previous snapshot.
+Restore first validates the backup file (it must be a usable SQLite database
+with the expected Harnie schema), then overwrites the live store with the
+backup contents. Restore has no undo: anything written after the backup is
+discarded.
